   │
15 │   result.flatten(result.map(parsed, check))
   │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ This maps a `Result` and then flattens it

`result.try` does both in one call: its docs say it "is the equivalent of
calling `map` followed by `flatten`", and it is the function `use` chains
fallible steps with.

Hint: Call `result.try(result, apply: fun)` in place of `result.map`, and
drop the `result.flatten`.

